@* One ruled block of the character sheet: a small-caps heading and its contents.

   It used to carry an `Empty`/`EmptyText` pair that printed "None." when a section had
   nothing in it. Nothing ever set them, and the behaviour they described is the one the
   sheet was rebuilt to get rid of: the reference is a *form*, so a character with no Perks
   prints a Perks box with room to write in it, not a box that says "None." — a sheet you
   cannot add a Perk to at the table is a report. `<RuledLines>` is what fills those boxes
   now. Do not bring the pair back; there is a test named for that regression. *@

<section class="@ClassName">
    @if (Title is not null)
    {
        <h3>@Title</h3>
    }
    @ChildContent
</section>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The heading, centred in a bar. Null for the two masthead boxes, which carry the
    /// character's name and the sheet's own title and would be captioned by neither.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Title { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    private string ClassName =>
        string.IsNullOrEmpty(Class) ? "sheet-section" : $"sheet-section {Class}";
}
